{"id": "EUVD-2026-108738", "enisaUuid": "e2740f47-0fdd-3192-9b89-aadf8732cf39", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv4: stop route notification sizing when nexthop group shrinks\n\nCommit 680aea08e78c (\"net: ipv4: Emit notification when fib\nhardware flags are changed\") added an RCU-only fib_nlmsg_size() call\nfor asynchronous hardware flag notifications.\n\nfib_nlmsg_size() checks fib_info_num_path() before each iteration,\nthen fib_info_nhc() independently reloads nh->nh_grp. If\nRTM_NEWNEXTHOP replaces a group with fewer paths between those loads,\nfib_info_nhc() returns NULL and fib_nexthop_nlmsg_size() dereferences\nit.\n\nStop sizing when the indexed path is absent. Nexthop groups are\ndense, so the current snapshot has no later path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72d9d17092bb37b0717f12042a0817d01a1f9e78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad1c9f1b98c92609e9bb2ae8f05916defc3b0a54", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1f48d1c2d5e9efd904dbbc2f2b3d41543e55c49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad2b3a68b8a7d5d27de88e05674e4adb1ce46d88", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3daa33c7af92e38f2274bbd2576f58bfbaf89e6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99072"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0998e5cd-3bf1-3e53-b681-c3a770267e7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "5b69e8cd-2051-39cf-b7e1-5ffc139923bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "680aea08e78c003292415518ad270bc20f9c80b1 <72d9d17092bb37b0717f12042a0817d01a1f9e78"}, {"id": "837f1940-1700-3e37-9564-28846591d71e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "ab0b8958-72bf-37f4-8db6-72b58efd0799", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_v